					>
						Read Report ↗
					</a>

					<a
						href="https://github.com/Shercroft/Graduate-Admission/blob/main/chance-of-admit-via-ann-lr.ipynb"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer"
					>
						View Notebook ↗
					</a>

				</div>

			</div>

		</div>

	</div>


	<!-- =====================================================
	     11 — TAKEAWAY
	===================================================== -->

	<div class="project-block">

		<div class="project-label">
			Takeaway
		</div>

		<div class="project-main">

			<h2>
				Use complexity when the problem earns it.
			</h2>

			<p class="lead">
				The main lesson was not that one class of models is
				universally better than another.
			</p>

			<p>
				Rather, model complexity should be evaluated relative to
				the structure of the data and the improvement it actually
				provides.
			</p>

			<p>
				On this task, logistic regression remained highly
				competitive with the neural network, demonstrating the
				value of establishing a strong statistical baseline before
				moving to a more complex architecture.
			</p>

		</div>

	</div>


